oth  republican senators losing their races  yeah 100 percent  absolutely uh and it was unfortunate uh  i don't claim to be smarter than anybody  by any stretch of the imagination i'm  just a retired baseball player for the  most part but i could see it coming from  a mile away  when they by by default hired donald  trump as their campaign manager during  the runoff  that was the beginning to the end  georgians wanted to be reminded of their  conservative policies and and positions  that they stood for they they you know  georgia fell in love with their business  acumen and their ability to articulate  jobs and you know national security and  all those things that really kind of are  the tenets of why you know we wanted  them there and why the governor  hand-selected kelly leffler to represent  johnny isaac since the the remainder of  his term  they forgot to do that and uh  unfortunately donald trump got his hooks  in him  and you know just made it all about him  and his conspiracy theories do you think  that trump's actions uh in terms of uh  the influence campaign and the phone  calls  might have been criminal  so i'm not an attorney i i told you i'm  a recovering baseball player  but based on conversations you have  there  yeah so look i i think i think i'll  start with they were absolutely  inappropriate  uh and they were disgusting uh whether i  was a whatever you know party  affiliations were associated with it  they were just inappropriate and uh i  know that there's investigations going  on and they're gonna certainly get to  the bottom of what their opinions are  from those legal uh investigations but i  don't have i don't have the legal acumen  to split hairs and know if it was  illegal or not it was inappropriate for  sure fair uh one of the the criticisms  i've had of the republican party of late  as someone who's not a republican is  that  the focus on policy has become close to  zero and the most prominent republicans  right now that that get headline